-- Example: schedule the nightly Stripe check.
--
-- Like the card check and room-count truing, this posts to the Next.js app,
-- not an Edge Function: it reads Stripe with the same client and writes
-- hotel_subscriptions through the same rules as the webhook
-- (src/lib/billing/reconcile.ts).
--
-- What it does, once a day: every subscription on record that is not over is
-- re-read from Stripe and MAYA's copy corrected, and a live subscription
-- created in the last 3 days that MAYA has no record of is recorded (a signup
-- whose messages from Stripe never arrived). Any difference other than a date
-- goes to the alert channel through the billing watchdog, because it means
-- Stripe's messages are not getting through. A run stops starting new reads
-- after 45 seconds and the next run carries on where it stopped.
--
-- Prereqs: extensions `pg_cron`, `pg_net`; Vault secrets. Reuses the SAME
-- billing_cron_secret and maya_app_url as the card check.
--
-- 0) Ensure extensions exist:
--    create extension if not exists pg_net;
--    create extension if not exists pg_cron;
--
-- 1) Secrets (both already exist if the card check is scheduled):
--    select vault.create_secret('https://maya.your-domain.com', 'maya_app_url');
--    select vault.create_secret('<long-random-string>', 'billing_cron_secret');
--
-- 2) App env (Vercel → Environment Variables, Production + Preview):
--    BILLING_CRON_SECRET, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY,
--    NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
--
-- 3) Schedule (08:40 UTC daily, away from room-count truing at 09:20):
--    select cron.schedule(
--      'billing-stripe-reconcile',
--      '40 8 * * *',
--      $$
--      select net.http_post(
--        url := (select decrypted_secret from vault.decrypted_secrets where name = 'maya_app_url')
--               || '/api/billing/reconcile',
--        headers := jsonb_build_object(
--          'Content-Type', 'application/json',
--          'x-billing-cron-secret', (select decrypted_secret from vault.decrypted_secrets where name = 'billing_cron_secret')
--        ),
--        body := jsonb_build_object('scheduled_at', now()),
--        timeout_milliseconds := 60000
--      ) as request_id;
--      $$
--    );
--
-- Inspect:    select jobid, jobname, schedule, active from cron.job;
-- Runs log:   select * from cron.job_run_details order by start_time desc limit 20;
-- Unschedule: select cron.unschedule('billing-stripe-reconcile');
--
-- What it found. Each run is a billing.sweep row, and each difference a
-- billing.problem row (key billing-drift:<hotel id>):
--   select event_type, entity_id, detail, created_at
--     from public.platform_audit_events
--    where (event_type = 'billing.sweep' and entity_id = 'stripe-reconcile')
--       or (event_type = 'billing.problem' and entity_id like 'billing-drift:%')
--    order by created_at desc limit 20;
